              <time datetime="2021-10-15T11:16:14Z">October 15, 2021</time>

<div class="field-html-title"><h4><a href="/media/before-after/mapping-roadways-landsat-scale" hreflang="en">Mapping Roadways at Landsat Scale</a></h4>
<a href="/media/before-after/mapping-roadways-landsat-scale" class="d-link" hreflang="en"><span class="hidden">Mapping Roadways at Landsat Scale</span></a></div>
  Mapping Roadways at Landsat Scale

<div class="field field--name--field-detailed-description field--type--text-long field--label--hidden">
    
      <div  class="field-detailed-description"><div class="tex2jax_process"><p>A satellite flying over this area northwest of Dallas, TX will capture a wide variety of urban and rural activity. The 80-odd square miles seen in the Landsat image on the left includes airports, dense urban centers, suburban and exurban neighborhoods, manufacturing and distribution centers, oil and gas production sites, lakes, forests, wetlands and more.</p></div></div>
  
</div>

<div class="field field--name--field-attributions field--type--computed-string-long field--label--inline">
      <div class="field-label">By</div>
    
      <div  class="field-attributions"><span class='attribution'><a href="/centers/eros" hreflang="en">Earth Resources Observation and Science (EROS) Center </a></span></div>
  
</div>

          </div>
        </div>

