<div class="field field--name--field-detailed-description field--type--text-long field--label--hidden">
    
      <div  class="field-detailed-description"><div class="tex2jax_process"><p>The National Land Cover Database, or NLCD, was the first and remains the most well-known set of satellite-based land cover mapping products released by EROS. It sorts the each 30-by-30-meter plot of land in the United States into a land cover class, such as cropland, pasture, high-intensity developed, deciduous forest, and the like.</p></div></div>
  
