  <div class="node node--type--news node--view-mode--teaser c-usgs-teaser">
  <div class="d-image" style="background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4)), url(&#039;https://d9-wret.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/assets/palladium/production/s3fs-public/styles/teaser/public/media/images/sagebrush%20banner%20photo.jpg?itok=HSYM-EiW&#039;) 50% 50% no-repeat; background-size: cover;">
    <a href="/centers/eros/news/maximizing-accuracy-rangeland-data" class="d-link"><span class="usa-sr-only">  Maximizing Accuracy of Rangeland Data
</span></a>
    <div class="d-title-info">
      <div class="d-info">  <time datetime="2024-04-03T21:49:05Z">April 3, 2024</time>

</div>
      <h4 class="d-title">  Maximizing Accuracy of Rangeland Data
</h4>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="d-teaser-body">
    
<div class="field field--name--field-intro field--type--text-long field--label--hidden">
  
      <div  class="field-intro">  <p>Project Manager Matthew Rigge and the Rangeland Condition Monitoring Assessment and Projection (RCMAP) team take an almost businesslike approach to...</p>

